      "description": "Watch Nantes vs RED Star FC 93 highlights and goals from Ligue 2 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. On August 8, 2026 , Nantes and Red Star FC 93 went head-to-head in a pivotal Ligue 2 fixture that promised high-intensity football. Both teams entered the pitch with clear tactical instructions, setting the stage for a compelling battle under the lights. A Cagey Opening Period The match began as a tactical chess match, with both sides prioritizing defensive solidity over expansive attacking play. Red Star FC 93 established a strong physical presence early on, which led to the first booking of the game in the 26th minute when Tylel Tati was shown a yellow card for a robust challenge. Nantes attempted to dictate the tempo through possession, but they struggled to break down a well-organized away defense. As the first half progressed, the frustration of the home side became palpable. In the 36th minute, Saif-Eddine Khaoui received a yellow card as the game became increasingly fragmented by fouls. Despite several half-chances at both ends, neither goalkeeper was truly tested before the referee blew for halftime, leaving the score locked at 0-0 in a display of discipline and grit. Cabral Strikes to Break the Deadlock The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to find a breakthrough. Nantes introduced fresh legs in the form of Jovany Ikanga A Ngele and Bahereba Guirassy just before the hour mark, but it was the visitors who would find the clinical edge. In the 67th minute, Elyaz Zidane delivered a perfectly weighted assist for Kevin Cabral , who made no mistake in slotting the ball home to give Red Star FC 93 a 1-0 lead. In the final twenty minutes, the atmosphere grew increasingly hostile. Nantes pushed forward in search of an equalizer, leading to a flurry of bookings, including one for Bahmed Deuff and another for manager Michel Der Zakarian . Red Star FC 93 showed remarkable resilience to weather the storm. Despite late yellow cards for Ryad Hachem and Cheick Konate during six minutes of stoppage time, the visitors held firm to secure a massive away victory and all three points."
